## 2c. New / additional env — use project env stack (Required)

When README, docs, or a feature adds **new** variables (not already in the project):

**MUST** wire them through the **existing project env system** — never ad-hoc `process.env.*` reads in routes, services, or components.

### Env naming (Required)

**MUST NOT** invent generic names (e.g. `NEW_VAR`, `MY_KEY`, `API_KEY_2`). Names **MUST** come from:

| Priority | Source |
|----------|--------|
| 1 | Exact name in **`README.md` / `docs/**`** (e.g. `FIGMA_TOKEN`, `CLICKUP_API_KEY`, `DB_NAME`) |
| 2 | Existing **`packages/config/src/env.js`** / `.env.example` in `{monorepo}` |
| 3 | Same pattern as sibling keys in that file (e.g. `GITHUB_TOKEN` next to `GITHUB_USERNAME`) |

- Reuse an **existing** project key when the integration is the same — do not duplicate under a new name.
- If docs use a different name than the repo, **align to the project** `.env.example` and note the doc alias in plan § Environment.
- Placeholder in rules/docs: `{ENV_KEY}` means “the real name from README/docs” — not a literal variable name.

### Before adding a key

| Check | Path |
|-------|------|
| Shared keys already defined? | `packages/config/src/env.js`, root `.env.example` |
| App-only keys? | `{backend_app}/src/config/env.js`, `{frontend_app}/src/config/env.js` |
| Standalone backend (no monorepo config)? | `{backend_app}/src/config/index.js` or `app/backend/src/config/index.js` |
| DB-related? | `applyProjectDatabaseEnv`, `database-common-stack.mdc`, `knexfile.js` |

### Add a new variable (all steps)

| Step | Action |
|------|--------|
| 1 | **Keep** all existing project env keys — new vars **extend** the stack, do not replace `loadEnv` / `@repo/config` |
| 2 | Add Joi entry in **`packages/config/src/env.js`** (shared) **or** `apps/{name}/src/config/env.js` (app-only) |
| 3 | Add row to root `.env.example` and/or app `.env.example` — value from README/docs; if **no value in docs**, empty OK **with comment** (§ 2b Empty value + comment) |
| 4 | Add to local `{monorepo}/.env` (gitignored) — **non-empty** if key required at boot; prod-only keys may stay unset locally when optional |
| 5 | If `DB_*` or platform key — follow § Database env priority + `{db_name}` rules |
| 6 | Call sites use `const { env } = require("./config/env")` — **not** raw `process.env` |
| 7 | Preview/webpack/proxy: ensure `loadEnv()` runs before `env` is read |
| 8 | Key already in plan `.md` from docs; update plan Value if user supplies one later |

### Shared vs app-only

| Key used by | Register in |
|-------------|-------------|
| API + web + scripts | `packages/config/src/env.js` + root `.env.example` |
| One app only | That app's `src/config/env.js` + app `.env.example` |
| Build-time browser (`DefinePlugin`) | `{frontend_app}/src/config/env.js` + webpack imports config only |

### Anti-patterns

```js
// ❌ FIGMA_TOKEN in .env only — never registered in env.js / config
const token = process.env.FIGMA_TOKEN;

// ❌ CLICKUP_API_KEY read in route — bypasses project env
router.get("/", () => fetch(process.env.CLICKUP_API_URL));

// ❌ Invented name not in README or .env.example
const x = process.env.MY_CUSTOM_API_KEY;

// ✅ Names from README/docs + packages/config or app config/env.js + .env.example
const { env } = require("./config/env");
fetch(env.CLICKUP_API_URL);
```

- **MUST** merge doc/README values **with** existing `.env.example` keys — do not drop platform vars (`PORT`, `DB_*`, `PUBLIC_PATH`) when adding feature env.
- **MUST** use **SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE** and **match names already used** in the project or documented in README/docs.

